Long: When opening some document types the renderer crashes with this uncaught exception in the main process. Trace:

Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length')
    at RendererComponent.renderDocument (file:///app/build/renderer.js:23345:27)
    at processImmediate (internal/timers.js:456:21)

Reproduction steps:
1. Open app
2. Import .customdoc file from legacy exporter
3. Select file in sidebar -> crash

Suspect the document loader returns null for missing fields. Please update the loader to return a well-typed Document | null and change renderDocument to handle null safely. Example types:

// types/document.ts
export interface Document {
  id: string;
  title?: string;
  content: string[]; // should be normalized
}

// loader.ts (current buggy snippet)
export async function loadDoc(path: string) {
  const raw = JSON.parse(await fs.promises.readFile(path, 'utf8'));
  return raw; // raw.content sometimes undefined
}

Please add normalization so content is always an array: raw.content = Array.isArray(raw.content) ? raw.content : [String(raw.content || '')]; and update unit tests.

Long: Intermittent 'IPC channel not registered' errors when renderer invokes main functions after hot-reload. Full error:

