Long: Memory leak in the preview worker after repeated file opens. Heap snapshots show many retained Closure scopes referencing large buffers. Worker code:

// src/main/previewWorker.ts
self.onmessage = (msg) => {
  const buffer = msg.data.buffer;
  const result = heavyProcess(buffer);
  postMessage({ result });
};

heavyProcess allocates multiple arrays and closures. Reproduction:
1. Open 100 large files via File -> Open
2. Observe process memory grows and never releases

Request: Refactor preview processing to reuse a worker pool and avoid capturing large buffers in closures. Example change:
- Use transferable objects with postMessage(buffer, [buffer])
- Ensure heavyProcess is pure and returns results without referencing outer scope
- Terminate workers after idle timeout

Please provide code changes and update tests to assert memory stays bounded in integration test (use max-old-space-size flag and validate peak memory).

