Long: When calling POST /api/orders clients are intermittently seeing 500 with this stack trace. Repro steps: submit two identical order payloads concurrently for the same cart id.

Stacktrace:
java.lang.NullPointerException: null
	at com.example.orders.OrderService.createOrder(OrderService.java:142)
	at com.example.orders.OrderController.create(OrderController.java:67)
	at java.base/jdk.internal.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke0(Native Method)

Investigation: Looks like orderNumberGenerator.getNext() sometimes returns null under high concurrency due to a lazy-initialized static field. Please refactor OrderNumberGenerator to be thread-safe (use AtomicLong or synchronized block) and add integration test that fires concurrent requests to ensure unique non-null order numbers. Example problematic code:

public class OrderNumberGenerator {
    private static Long last;

    public Long getNext() {
        if (last == null) {
            last = loadFromDb();
        }
        last = last + 1;
        return last;
    }
}

Replace with AtomicLong and synchronized initialization.

Long: After upgrading Jackson we started seeing failures deserializing polymorphic DTOs used by the API. Error:
