Long: API gateway is stripping custom headers like X-Request-ID and X-Client-Version causing loss of tracing. Example of header missing in backend logs. Edge stack uses Apache httpd proxy with ProxyPassReverse. We need to preserve headers and forward them. Suggested changes: set ProxyPreserveHost On, add 'RequestHeader unset Proxy' adjustments, and in Spring set ForwardedHeaderFilter or configure Tomcat's RemoteIpValve to respect X-Forwarded-* headers. Also update API to set requestId if missing: in OncePerRequestFilter:

String requestId = req.getHeader("X-Request-ID");
if (requestId == null) requestId = UUID.randomUUID().toString();
MDC.put("requestId", requestId);
resp.setHeader("X-Request-ID", requestId);

Add integration test that sends header through gateway and asserts it's present in backend.

